ng, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu Credit: Anna Logue University Academics After Your Studies Career Opportunities Career Opportunities Some prospective students settle for a degree program because they are very enthusiastic about a certain field and only think about possible professions later. Others know right from the start where they want to work later and choose their studies accordingly. Regardless of how it is for you, one thing is certain: with a master’s degree from the University of Mannheim, you have excellent career opportunities—this is confirmed by numerous rankings and surveys among HR managers. We provide you an overview on possible careers, continuing education, and career assistance services. Credit: Anna Logue and Daniela Haupt Careers of Mannheim Graduates A degree program is not tailored to a certain profession. Benefit from the experiences our graduates made. Credit: blende 11 Fotografen Studying at the University of Mannheim laid an important foundation for my professional career. Not only did I acquire subject-specific knowledge but also project management skills, communication techniques, and effective strategies for exploring new topics. These skills have proven to be valuable for my daily work and helped me to achieve my current position. Florian Kuczera, HR manager, graduate of Economic and Business Education Credit: Sandra Blossey In my jobs, I have repeatedly found that the multifaceted degree program taught me to think outside the box and to combine a wide range of disciplines. Jessica Nollmann, Head of Organizational Development and Internal Communications, graduate of English and American Studies Credit: Fotografie Gaby Höss Internships and commitment outside of the university are important and valuable. Establishing a professional network is key. It will help recent graduates in search of their first job. Paul Beck, Coordinator at the Federal Ministry of Finance, Law graduate Credit: Christian Kaufmann Many successful people have had a career that has been marked by detours as well as ups and downs. Accept that your career is not always straightforward, and think of obstacles as a chance to find the right place in your “new” job. Dr. Philipp Laux, independent coach and team psychologist at BVB, Psychology graduate Credit: blende 11 Fotografen Studying at the University of Mannheim laid an important foundation for my professional career. Not only did I acquire subject-specific knowledge but also project management skills, communication techniques, and effective strategies for exploring new topics. These skills have proven to be valuable for my daily work and helped me to achieve my current position. Florian Kuczera, HR manager, graduate of Economic and Business Education Credit: Sandra Blossey In my jobs, I have repeatedly found that the multifaceted degree program taught me to think outside the box and to combine a wide range of disciplines. Jessica Nollmann, Head of Organizational Development and Internal Communications, graduate of English and American Studies Credit: Fotografie Gaby Höss Internships and commitment outside of the university are important and valuable. Establishing a professional network is key. It will help recent graduates in search of their first job. Paul Beck, Coordinator at the Federal Ministry of Finance, Law graduate Credit: Christian Kaufmann Many successful people have had a career that has been marked by detours as well as ups and downs. Accept that your career is not always straightforward, and think of obstacles as a chance to find the right place in your “new” job. Dr. Philipp Laux, independent coach and team psychologist at BVB, Psychology graduate Credit: blende 11 Fotografen Studying at the University of Mannheim laid an important foundation for my professional career. Not only did I acquire subject-specific knowledge but also project management skills, communication techniques, and effective strategies for exploring new topics. These skills have proven to be valuable for my daily work and helped me to achieve my current position. Florian Kuczera, HR manager, graduate of Economic and Business Education 1 2 3 4 Credit: Anna Logue Fields of Work With a degree from the University of Mannheim, you are qualified for many jobs in various industries. We provide a list of possible fields of work so you can get an overview. Credit: Felix Zeiffer Job Opportunities A degree from the University of Mannheim promises great job opportunities. Learn more about university rankings and what HR experts say. Credit: Anna Logue Practical Experience Gaining practical experience during your studies helps you find the right career and land your first job after university. Get an overview on the internship and job databases. Credit: Anna Logue Starting Your Career The university continues to support you after graduation and helps you find a job. Learn more about the mentoring program, the CV check, the consultation hour for start-ups and other services. A career in academia or research Credit: Anna Logue Are you interested in pursuing a career in academia or research after your graduation? Numerous opportunities are available at the University of Mannheim to help you along your professional path. If you graduated from the University of Mannheim, you are qualified to start an academic or research career . Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment Opportunities FORUM The University of Mannheim's magazine + Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde Universität Mannheim Absolventum Mannheim Scholarships Contact About This Site Data Protection Declaration Barrierefreiheit Sitemap House Rules Safety and Emergencies Instagram Page of the University of Mannheim Facebook Page of the University of Mannheim LinkedIn Page of the University of Mannheim Tiktok Page of the University of Mannheim YouTube Page of the University of Mannheim Mastodon Page of the University of Mannheim In order to improve performance and enhance the user experience for the visitors to our website, we use cookies and store anonymous usage data. For more information please read our privacy policy . Allow Reject Tracking cookies are currently allowed. Do not allow tracking cookies Tracking cookies are currently not allowed. Allow tracking cookies × How would you like to open the file? Remember for next time View PDF document Download PDF document"
    },
