e University Vocational Training, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu Credit: Anna Logue University Academics After Your Studies Career Opportunities Fields of Work Political Science Political Science Career prospects for graduates A degree in Political Science qualifies you for jobs that require empirical-analytical work and the application of quantitative methods. You can either work in the public service or in the private sector. There is no set career path for social scientists. Instead, students specialize in their studies through internships, part-time jobs, or volunteer work, which helps to hone their individual profiles. Potential careers The list below provides you with a brief overview on potential professions: Consulting In both public and private organizations, political scientists can give recommendations for action based on analyses they previously conducted. For example, they develop new business models and services or create communication strategies. Communication In the area of public affairs, political scientists engage in foreign relations and work for agencies, political parties, or administrations. They strategically communicate with different groups (e.g., citizens, political decision-makers, associations, or NGOs) in order to advance the interests of their principal. Political Institutions Graduates can assume a political office, consult on a scientific basis, or prepare decisions in governmental institutions such as the European Parliament or the German Bundestag. Political scientists can also become press officers of a political party, where they respond to citizens’ inquiries, issue press statements, newsletter articles and social media posts, or are responsible for the conceptual preparation and organization of new dialog formats. Academia If you complete a master’s degree, you can pursue an academic career. The master’s program in Political Science is the perfect choice if you plan to continue your academic training with a doctoral program in order to pursue a career in science and research . Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment