es Benefits Job Insights – Working at the University Vocational Training, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu Credit: Emilie Orgler University Academics After Your Studies Career Opportunities Fields of Work Mathematics in Business and Economics Mathematics in Business and Economics Career prospects for graduates With knowledge of a combination of fields, mathematics, business administration and economics , you have a wide range of career options. Apart from starting a job after the bachelor’s program, you can also continue your studies in the master’s program in Mathematics in Business and Economics (M.Sc.) , the Mannheim Master of Data Science (M.Sc.) or the Mannheim Master in Management (M.Sc.) programs. Potential careers With a degree in Mathematics in Business and Economics you can pursue the following careers, among others: Business Potential employers in this area are: Accounting firms Banks Insurance companies Financial service providers Business consultancies IT companies Software development companies Job titles: Analysts (financial, investment, operational analysis) look into current and future investments and processes, and subsequently evaluate and optimize them. Actuaries use mathematical and statistical models to predict incidents that could have a financial impact on a company. Business or IT consultants advise managers on problem solving and the implementation of new business approaches by using mathematical models and methods. Science and research Scientists in the field of mathematics in business and economics research theoretical and practical topics by applying their mathematical knowledge and methods, such as stochastic simulation, signal processing, and numerical analysis. The master’s program in Mathematics in Business and Economics is the perfect choice if you plan to continue your academic training with a doctoral program in order to pursue a career in science and research . Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment Opportunities FORUM The University of Mannheim's magazine + Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde Un