ity Vocational Training, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu Credit: Anna Logue University Academics After Your Studies Career Opportunities Practical Experience Practical Experience You can gain practical experience during your studies by doing internships , working student jobs , or getting involved in one of various student organizations . This will help you find out which profession best matches your skills and interests. Many companies and organizations also place a high value on practical experience. Jobs and internships Credit: Anna Logue If you are looking for a job or an internship, job databases are a good starting point. You can also send unsolicited applications, which is often a good option if you are already considering a specific company or organization. to the internship and job databases Student organizations and departmental student committees Credit: Anna Logue An asset of the University of Mannheim is its large variety of student organizations . Many of the student organizations work to provide students a head start in their careers or insight into different professions. In other student organizations and departmental student committees, you can already gain hands-on experience during your studies, for example, by organizing major events or assisting children and young adults. to the student organizations focusing on professional careers (in German) Field-specific jobs and internships Humanities The School of Humanities provides information about internships in Germany and abroad on their website. You can also search the internship and job database for a variety of field-specific opportunities, such as PR traineeships, internships in online journalism, or working student jobs. opportunities at the School of Humanities Business Administration The Business School has many contacts in the industry. Therefore, it can offer a wide variety of internships, working student positions, and jobs. to the internship and job database of the Business School Law Mannheim Law students are provided with many opportunities to gain valuable practical experience. The Department of Law provides information about the Career Day, internship and job databases, mentoring programs, and the Career Network. opportunities at the Department of Law Mathematics and Informatics The School of Business Informatics and Mathematics compiled information on the career fair, internships and jobs, the mentoring program, and the Career Network. opportunities at the School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Social Sciences After graduating from university, social sciences students can pursue a career in a variety of fields. But already during their studies they can start preparing for their career. gain practical experience in the social sciences Economics The Department of Economics collected information about stays abroad, internships, and advisory services. information for Economics students Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment Opportunities FORUM The University of Mannheim's magazine + Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde Universität Mannheim Absolventum Mannheim Scholarships Contact About This Site Data Protection Declaration Barrierefreiheit Sitemap House Rules Safety and Emergencies Instagram Page of the University of Mannheim Facebook Page of the University of Mannheim LinkedIn Page of the University of Mannheim Tiktok Page of the University of Mannheim YouTube Page of the University of Mannheim Mastodon Page of the University of Mannheim In order to improve performance and enhance the user experience for the visitors to our website, we use cookies and store anonymous usage data. For more information please read our privacy policy . Allow Reject Tracking cookies are currently allowed. Do not allow tracking cookies Tracking cookies are currently not allowed. Allow tracking cookies × How would you like to open the file? Remember for next time View PDF document Download PDF document"
