ng at the University Vocational Training, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu Credit: Anna Logue University Academics Coming to Mannheim International Degree-Seeking Students Starting Your Career Starting Your Career The programs of study at the University of Mannheim will prepare international degree-seeking students for a career in many different fields of work. You can already gain practical experience during your studies at the university itself or at one of the numerous prestigious companies in the region. As an international graduate, the world will be your oyster! We will assist you in navigating the German labor market. The project Made in Mannheim – FIT for Career offers workshops and training. These are an addition to the services offered by the CareerNetwork and are tailored to your needs. Credit: Anna Logue Made in Mannheim – FIT for Career Do you want to work while studying, are you looking for an internship or do you plan to pursue a career in Germany after completing your studies? Take advantage of the workshops and events offered by the program Made in Mannheim – FIT for Career! Credit: Anna Logue International alumni Have you already successfully completed your studies? Then become a member of ABSOLVENTUM, participate in our AlumniNight, and keep in touch! Contact: Credit: Katrin Glückler Miriam Kucher (she/her) Advisor Career Entry International Degree-Seeking Students, Coordinator Made in Mannheim – FIT for Career University of Mannheim Division II – Student Affairs International Office L 1, 1 – Room 109 68161 Mannheim Phone: +49 621 181-1440 E-mail: miriam.kucher @ uni-mannheim.de Consultation hour(s): Please book an appointment for an individual consultation with me at https://www.uni-mannheim.de/en/about/centers-institutions-affiliates-and-partners/international-office ... Office hours: Visit my office without an appointment during our open office hours on Tuesdays from 9 to 11 a.m. For questions on working as an international student, meet me online without an appointment on Mondays from 1:30 to 3 p.m. at https://uni-mannheim.zoom-x.de/j/65836831088?pwd=Z1IQgFfialmNjsqkm63jIZyO99aazw.1 Credit: Ye Fung Tchen International Office Directions on Google Maps © OpenMapTiles © OpenStreetMap contributors International Office University of Mannheim Division II – Student Affairs L 1, 1 (1. OG) 68161 Mannheim Phone: +49 621 181-2222 Fax: +49 621 181-1161 E-mail: io @ uni-mannheim.de Web: www.uni-mannheim.de/io Consultation hour(s): Tue 9 a.m. – 11 a.m. and by appointment Facebook Page Instagram Page Linkedin Page YouTube Page Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment Opportunities FORUM The University of Mannheim's magazine + Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde Universität Mannheim Absolventum Mannheim Scholarships Contact About This Site Data Protection Declaration Barrierefreiheit Sitemap House Rules Safety and Emergencies Instagram Page of the University of Mannheim Facebook Page of the University of Mannheim LinkedIn Page of the University of Mannheim Tiktok Page of the University of Mannheim YouTube Page of the University of Mannheim Mastodon Page of the University of Mannheim In order to improve performance and enhance the user experience for the visitors to our website, we use cookies and store anonymous usage data. For more information please read our privacy policy . Allow Reject Tracking cookies are currently allowed. Do not allow tracking cookies Tracking cookies are currently not allowed. Allow tracking cookies × How would you like to open the file? Remember for next time View PDF document Download PDF document"
