ights – Working at the University Vocational Training, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu Credit: Anna Logue University Academics Coming to Mannheim International Degree-Seeking Students Starting Your Career Made in Mannheim Made in Mannheim – FIT for Career We want to support you in planning your career and make sure you feel prepared for entering the (German) job market after your graduation. Each semester, we host various events that are designed to help you start your career as part of our DAAD-funded program Made in Mannheim – FIT for Career – an offer which exclusively addresses our international degree-seeking students. Please note: Registration is required for all events. We will inform you via e-mail once the registration starts. To ensure fair access to our events and make responsible use of resources such as catering and external speakers, there will be a new attendance policy for all Made in Mannheim events with limited spaces, starting with the fall semester 2026: Participants who cancel their registration less than 24 hours before the event or fail to attend without a valid excuse will be barred from registering for all Made in Mannheim events for one month. A second unexcused absence will result in exclusion from all Made in Mannheim events for the remainder of the semester. We appreciate your understanding and cooperation. We would like to point out that, as part of our reporting obligations to the DAAD, we are required to report the following personal data about you to the DAAD in anonymized form: gender and nationality All HWS events at a glance Offer When? What can you expect? German courses: German@Work once a week during lecture period (see below) German@Work is exclusively designed for international students in English-taught degree programs who want to start their career in Germany. German@Work A1.1 Mondays, 1:30 to 4 p.m. German language lessons with vocational focus comprising 4 teaching units per week (3 in-class units + 1 Moodle unit) German@Work A1.2 Wednesdays, 1:45 to 4:15 p.m. German language lessons with vocational focus comprising 4 teaching units per week (3 in-class units + 1 Moodle unit) German@Work A2.1 Fridays, 8 to 10:30 a.m. German language lessons with vocational focus comprising 4 teaching units per week (3 in-class units + 1 Moodle unit) German@Work A2.2 Fridays, 11:15 a.m. to 2:45 p.m. German language lessons with vocational focus comprising 4 teaching units per week (3 in-class units + 1 Moodle unit) German@Work B1.1 Thursdays, 5:15 to 7:45 p.m. German language lessons with vocational focus comprising 4 teaching units per week (3 in-class units + 1 Moodle unit) German@Work B1.2 Mondays, 5:15 to 7:45 p.m. German language lessons with vocational focus comprising 4 teaching units per week (3 in-class units + 1 Moodle unit) German@Work B2.1 Wednesdays, 1:45 to 4:15 p.m. German language lessons with vocational focus comprising 4 teaching units per week (3 in-class units + 1 Moodle unit) German@Work B2.2 Tuesdays, 1:45 to 4:15 p.m. German language lessons with vocational focus comprising 4 teaching units per week (3 in-class units + 1 Moodle unit) Confident and mentally strong in the application process Monday, 28 September, 10 a.m. to 1 p.m. Applying for jobs can be really challenging at the moment: Rejections, high pressure to succeed, and uncertainty about what German employers expect can quickly lead to stress, self-doubt, and feeling overwhelmed. This online workshop helps you to gain clarity about your personal profile and to identify your key strengths.  You learn how to present your skill set clearly in your CV and job interviews. At the same time, you will create more structure in your application process and strengthen your mental resilience. Intensive Application Training Thursday, 22 October and Thursday, 29 October, 3:30 to 5 p.m. This two-day workshop is offered in cooperation with Welcome Center Rhein-Neckar and looks in detail at the different steps of the application process. In practical exercises, you will learn how to use job portals for your systematic job search and how to interpret job postings correctly. You will also work on your application documents and even draft an individual cover letter for a current job opening with the trainer’s support. Language of event is English. Individual CV Checks tba Our 30-minutes online coaching address those who are currently in the application process and updating their resume for companies in Germany. In a 1:1 session, you get detailed feedback on language, layout and content of your CV and learn about German peculiarities in CV writing from an expert. Your CV can be in English OR German. International Alumni Night #backintown Wednesday, 4 November, 6 to 9 p.m. Get inspired by the success stories of our international graduates and expand your professional network. Language of event is English. Job Interview Training Friday, 20 November The training provides strategies on how to prepare for a job interview in terms of content and addresses additional aspects which might require your attention in such a setting. These include general appearance, outfit, body language etc. as well as specific German peculiarities. You also get the chance to simulate a job interview and receive professional feedback from the trainer right away. Language of event is English. ENGAGE.EU Career guidance platform Discover the ENGAGE.EU Career guidance platform and take your next professional step with confidence! Whether you are crafting your elevator pitch, exploring your strength s, or preparing for an international career , ENGAGE.EU provides tailored e-learning modules , expert country insights , and a wide range of inspiring career events . From CV and LinkedIn workshops to motivation‑letter trainings and masterclasses across partner universities, you will find everything you need to shape your future. Start building your career today! Participating in the Step by Step workshop was the best decision I made during my studies in Mannheim. Not only did I learn something valuable and useful for my future profession, but I also received helpful feedback on what I can improve in order to have better job opportunities in Germany and to integrate better into German society. All foreigners share the same concerns due to worries about the future and problems associated with integration. Workshops like the ones of Step by Step help us all to overcome these problems. Valeria Lebedieva from the Ukraine, student of the bachelor's program in Psychology International students obviously need a lot of support when making the transition to a new country. The Step by Step program offered by the International Office helped me a lot with understanding German culture and working environment. The various events offered range from “Applying for Internships” to “International Students & Taxation”. The Step by Step initiative comprehensively covers the needs of International students! Vishal Sharma from India, student of the Mannheim Master in Management (MMM) / Foto NN Participating in the Step by Step workshop was the best decision I made during my studies in Mannheim. Not only did I learn something valuable and useful for my future profession, but I also received helpful feedback on what I can improve in order to have better job opportunities in Germany and to integrate better into German society. All foreigners share the same concerns due to worries about the future and problems associated with integration. Workshops like the ones of Step by Step help us all to overcome these problems. Valeria Lebedieva from the Ukraine, student of the bachelor's program in Psychology International students obviously need a lot of support when making the transition to a new country. The Step by Step program offered by the International Office helped me a lot with understanding German culture and working environment. The various events offered range from “Applying for Internships” to “International Students & Taxation”. The Step by Step initiative comprehensively covers the needs of International students! Vishal Sharma from India, student of the Mannheim Master in Management (MMM) / Foto NN Participating in the Step by Step workshop was the best decision I made during my studies in Mannheim. Not only did I learn something valuable and useful for my future profession, but I also received helpful feedback on what I can improve in order to have better job opportunities in Germany and to integrate better into German society. All foreigners share the same concerns due to worries about the future and problems associated with integration. Workshops like the ones of Step by Step help us all to overcome these problems. Valeria Lebedieva from the Ukraine, student of the bachelor's program in Psychology 1 2 Stay in touch! Stay in touch with the University of Mannheim after graduating and make new contacts as alumnus/ a. Make use of the networking opportunities in the course of your career entry. Contact: Credit: Katrin Glückler Miriam Kucher (she/her) Advisor Career Entry International Degree-Seeking Students, Coordinator Made in Mannheim – FIT for Career University of Mannheim Division II – Student Affairs International Office L 1, 1 – Room 109 68161 Mannheim Phone: +49 621 181-1440 E-mail: miriam.kucher @ uni-mannheim.de Consultation hour(s): Please book an appointment for an individual consultation with me at https://www.uni-mannheim.de/en/about/centers-institutions-affiliates-and-partners/international-office ... Office hours: Visit my office without an appointment during our open office hours on Tuesdays from 9 to 11 a.m. For questions on working as an international student, meet me online without an appointment on Mondays from 1:30 to 3 p.m. at https://uni-mannheim.zoom-x.de/j/65836831088?pwd=Z1IQgFfialmNjsqkm63jIZyO99aazw.1 Credit: Ye Fung Tchen International Office Directions on Google Maps © OpenMapTiles © OpenStreetMap contributors International Office University of Mannheim Division II – Student Affairs L 1, 1 (1. OG) 68161 Mannheim Phone: +49 621 181-2222 Fax: +49 621 181-1161 E-mail: io @ uni-mannheim.de Web: www.uni-mannheim.de/io Consultation hour(s): Tue 9 a.m. – 11 a.m. and by appointment Facebook Page Instagram Page Linkedin Page YouTube Page Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment Opportunities FORUM The University of Mannheim's magazine + Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde Universität Mannheim Absolventum Mannheim Scholarships Contact About This Site Data Protection Declaration Barrierefreiheit Sitemap House Rules Safety and Emergencies Instagram Page of the University of Mannheim Facebook Page of the University of Mannheim LinkedIn Page of the University of Mannheim Tiktok Page of the University of Mannheim YouTube Page of the University of Mannheim Mastodon Page of the University of Mannheim In order to improve performance and enhance the user experience for the visitors to our website, we use cookies and store anonymous usage data. For more information please read our privacy policy . Allow Reject Tracking cookies are currently allowed. Do not allow tracking cookies Tracking cookies are currently not allowed. Allow tracking cookies × How would you like to open the file? Remember for next time View PDF document Download PDF document"
