s Benefits Job Insights – Working at the University Vocational Training, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu University Academics Coming to Mannheim International Degree-Seeking Students Starting Your Career Information for Companies Information for Companies The project STEP by STEP supports international students at the University of Mannheim in starting their career in the Rhine-Neckar Metropolitan Region. We want to connect students and companies through company visits. It is an opportunity for students to get to know potential employers and experience the economic strength of the region first-hand. Companies, on the other hand, have the unique chance to meet our highly skilled international students and present themselves as an attractive place of employment. This is how you can support us: Company visits Invite a group of international students to visit your company. Show the production facilitates during a tour of your plant, provide students with the chance to discuss career opportunities with your employees and let the students know what you are looking for in an application. What is included in a visit like this depends on the company’s resources and main focus and will of course be determined individually. Company presentations Speak at the University of Mannheim and present your company and what you are looking for in future employees. Due to our academic calendar, presentations are best held in March, April or May in the spring semester and in September, October or November in the fall semester. We are always interested in establishing new relationships with companies from all sectors and are looking forward to hearing from you ! Contact: Credit: Ye Fung Tchen International Office Directions on Google Maps © OpenMapTiles © OpenStreetMap contributors International Office University of Mannheim Division II – Student Affairs L 1, 1 (1. OG) 68161 Mannheim Phone: +49 621 181-2222 Fax: +49 621 181-1161 E-mail: io @ uni-mannheim.de Web: www.uni-mannheim.de/io Consultation hour(s): Tue 9 a.m. – 11 a.m. and by appointment Facebook Page Instagram Page Linkedin Page YouTube Page Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ..