ational Office As part of the project Made in Mannheim – FIT for Career the International Office is regularly hosting AlumniNights. At these events, successful international graduates talk about how they started their career in Germany and share their experiences with currently enrolled international students. Afterwards, an informal get-together gives all participants the opportunity to network and offer or ask advice personally. Please see the current Made in Mannheim – FIT for Career semester program for more information. If you are an international graduate of the University of Mannheim and are interested in keeping in contact with other former or current international students, get in touch with us ! Tell us where your career path has taken you. We are always looking for success stories to be told at our alumni events. We also generally enjoy hearing from you! ABSOLVENTUM As a member of the ABSOLVENTUM alumni network of the University of Mannheim, the largest alumni organization in Germany, you are part of an international network that offers many opportunities and brings you into contact with like-minded alumni. LinkedIn Become a member of our LinkedIn group for international students and graduates . Stay in touch with the university after you’ve graduated! Credit: Ye Fung Tchen International Office Directions on Google Maps © OpenMapTiles © OpenStreetMap contributors International Office University of Mannheim Division II – Student Affairs L 1, 1 (1. OG) 68161 Mannheim Phone: +49 621 181-2222 Fax: +49 621 181-1161 E-mail: io @ uni-mannheim.de Web: www.uni-mannheim.de/io Consultation hour(s): Tue 9 a.m. – 11 a.m. and by appointment Facebook Page Instagram Page Linkedin Page YouTube Page Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press R