t the University Vocational Training, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu Credit: Staatliche Schlösser und Gärten Baden-Württemberg University Research Postdoctoral Research Phase Postdoc Career Academy Postdoc Fund data protection Information on Data Protection on applying for funds from the Postdoc Fund of the University of Mannheim I. Identity and contact details of the controller The controller within the meaning of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is: University of Mannheim L1,1 68131 Mannheim Phone: 0621/ -181-1001 E-mail: rektor @ uni-mannheim.de II. Contact details of the data protection officer Data Protection Officer of the University of Mannheim Jan Morgenstern Lawyer and IT law specialist E-mail: datenschutzbeauftragter @ uni-mannheim.de III. Contact details of the executing entity Division I – Research Services and Quality Management L1, 1 68131 Mannheim Phone: 0621-181-1050 E-mail: postdocs @ uni-mannheim.de IV. General information on data processing 1. Purpose of data processing The Postdocs Fund is intended to enable postdocs to realize their own ideas in research and teaching. To this end, postdocs can apply for funds of up to 5,000 euros per year, which they can dispose of freely and independently of their supervisors. The data collected during the application process is used to process the applications. Applications cannot be processed without this data. We will anonymize your personal data as soon as and insofar as this is possible in accordance with the purpose pursued in each case. The transfer of data to third parties (e.g. reporting obligations to the responsible vice president/ president's office) will also only take place in anonymized form. 2. Legal basis for data processing The legal basis for the processing of your personal data is Article 6 paragraph 1 (e) in conjunction with paragraph 3 GDPR in conjunction with Article 12 paragraph 1 (1) in conjunction with Article 2 Act on Higher Education of the Land of Baden-Württemberg (LHG) in conjunction with Articles 70, 75 Landeshaushaltsordnung für Baden-Württemberg (LHO). 3. Type of data The following data will be processed for the application, the selection decision and the processing of the grant: name (first name & surname), school or institution, department, university e-mail address, amount of the requested funds, purpose of the requested fund. 4. Recipients of the data If there are any doubts regarding the eligibility of your project or your eligibility to apply, the decision on the application lies with the Vice president for Research and Academic Career Paths. The following data will be sent to them for this purpose: name (first name & surname), school or institution, department, university e-mail address, amount of the requested funds, purpose of the requested fund. In accordance with archiving regulations, we must offer documents to the University Archives before they are deleted. The archive then decides whether to accept the documents. 5. Storage period Division I and the responsible Vice President delete the data no later than five years after the funding decision. If necessary, the documents will be taken over by the responsible university archive and generally stored there indefinitely. V. Rights of the data subject 1. Your rights You have the right to request information about your personal data processed by us in accordance with Article 15 GDPR, demand the immediate correction of incorrect or incomplete personal data stored by us in accordance with Article 16 GDPR, request the erasure of your personal data stored by us in accordance with Article 17 GDPR, request the restriction of the processing of your personal data in accordance with Article 18 GDPR; to exercise your rights as a data subject, please contact: postdocs @ uni-mannheim.de , lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority in accordance with Article 77 GDPR. The supervisory authority in Baden-Württemberg is the State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information Baden-Württemberg (Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit Baden-Württemberg). 2. Right to object If your personal data is processed on the basis of Article 6 paragraph 1 (e) GDPR (data processing in the public interest), you have the right to object to the processing of your personal data in accordance with Article 21 GDPR, provided that there are reasons for this arising from your particular situation. If you would like to exercise your right to object, please send an email to postdocs @ uni-mannheim.de . Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment Opportunities FORUM The University of Mannheim's magazine + Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde Universität Mannheim Absolventum Mannheim Scholarships Contact About This Site Data Protection Declaration Barrierefreiheit Sitemap House Rules Safety and Emergencies Instagram Page of the University of Mannheim Facebook Page of the University of Mannheim LinkedIn Page of the University of Mannheim Tiktok Page of the University of Mannheim YouTube Page of the University of Mannheim Mastodon Page of the University of Mannheim In order to improve performance and enhance the user experience for the visitors to our website, we use cookies and store anonymous usage data. For more information please read our privacy policy . Allow Reject Tracking cookies are currently allowed. Do not allow tracking cookies Tracking cookies are currently not allowed. Allow tracking cookies × How would you like to open the file? Remember for next time View PDF document Download PDF document"
