he University Vocational Training, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu Credit: Staatliche Schlösser und Gärten Baden-Württemberg University Research Postdoctoral Research Phase Postdoc Career Academy Internationalization Internationalization Whether it is a short trip to an international conference or a longer research stay with a project partner abroad – we will support your international mobility to ensure that you can take part in international research activities. We believe that international mobility will provide you with new opportunities for your research work, keep you up to date, and help you network with countless fascinating researchers from all over the world. Researching has never been as global as it is today; become a part of it! Credit: ENGAGE.EU International Networking ENGAGE.EU is an alliance of leading European higher education institutions from the fields of Economics and Business Administration as well as Social Sciences, dedicated to addressing the societal challenges of our time. The alliance offers researchers numerous opportunities for networking and collaboration. Credit: Anna Logue Teaching Abroad The University of Mannheim wants to make teaching and research even more international. By completing an ERASMUS+ teaching or training placement, researchers from the University of Mannheim can, for example, gain experience at a European partner university, share approaches and content with international colleagues, and take good ideas back home with them. Contact Dr. Jayana Jain (she/her) Coordinator, Postdoc Career Academy Research Support, Academic Career Paths, Interdisciplinary Support and Counselling for Postdocs and Junior Professors University of Mannheim Divison I – Research Services and Quality Management L 1, 1 L1, 1 – Room 328 68161 Mannheim Phone: +49 621 181-1018 E-mail: jayana.jain @ uni-mannheim.de Web: Postdoc Career Academy Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment Opportunities FORUM The University of Mannheim's magazine + Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde Universität Mannheim Absolventum Mannhei