degree or are about to start your career: We are happy to advise you on your individual career development. Our advice is designed to understand your individual needs and goals and to assist you in achieving them. Counseling sessions are strictly confidential, open and unbiased as to the result. Potential decisions and solutions are not presented to you in advance, rather you will be encouraged to develop them yourself. We will support you in defining your professional goals, determining your status quo, and planning the best path for your academic career. Possible counseling topics may include: Orientation after completing your doctoral degree How to become a professor Analyzing your potential Programs for career advancement Check of application documents Contact Dr. Jayana Jain (she/her) Coordinator, Postdoc Career Academy Research Support, Academic Career Paths, Interdisciplinary Support and Counselling for Postdocs and Junior Professors University of Mannheim Divison I – Research Services and Quality Management L 1, 1 L1, 1 – Room 328 68161 Mannheim Phone: +49 621 181-1018 E-mail: jayana.jain @ uni-mannheim.de Web: Postdoc Career Academy Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment Opportunities FORUM The University of Mannheim's magazine + Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde Universität Mannheim Absolventum Mannheim Scholarships Contact About This Site Data Protection Declaration Barrierefreiheit Sitemap House Rules Safety and Emergencies Instagram Page of the University of Mannheim Facebook Page of the University of Mannheim LinkedIn Page of the University of Mannheim Tiktok Page of the University of Mannheim 