g Education and Qualification UMA Doc & Postdoc Days 2026 Anmeldung Doc & Postdoc Days Events for Doctoral Students Doctoral Students' Councils Advisory Services Individual Counseling Services Advising in Cases of Conflict Pursuing a Doctorate under Special Circumstances Promoting Female Researchers Important Downloads Postdoctoral Research Phase Postdoc Career Academy Postdoctoral Research Phase Funding Opportunities Continued Academic Training Postdoc Fund data protection Internationalization Grants for Travel Expenses Advice and Services Advice on Career Opportunities for Postdocs Conflicts Finding an Expert Campus The Schloss Schneckenhof Mannheim Living in Mannheim Neighborhoods in the city of Mannheim Getting Around in Mannheim myUniMA story Student Organizations and Departmental Student Committees Student Organizations Departmental Student Committees Sports Eating and Drinking Music, Theater, and Art Exhibitions and Art Upcoming Exhibitions Uni-Fest Safety and Emergencies About History Newsroom Media Relations Press Releases Press Photos Finding an Expert Newsletter, publications and social media Contact Newsletter Subscription Service News Newsletter FORUM Bulletin of the President's Office Events Profile Rankings Facts and Figures External Funding Strategy Diversity Sustainability Transfer Digitalization bwUni.digital Campus Extension Around Friedrichspark History Institutions and Schools Organization President's Office President's Office Communications Department Marketing Department Bodies and Committees University Supervisory Board Senate Committees and Councils Elections to the Bodies Schedule of Meetings Administration Legal Division Division I Division II Division III Division IV Division V Division VI Service Units Department of Safety and Security Data Protection Equal Opportunity and Diversity Teaching and Learning Center Representatives Data Protection Officer International ENGAGE.EU U7+ Working at the University Job Vacancies Benefits Job Insights – Working at the University Vocational Training, Cooperative Study Program, Internship Internship Training Provider in Cooperative Study Programs Cooperative Study Program in Computer Science Cooperative Study Program in Business Informatics Cooperative Study Program in Digital Business Management Vocational Training Media and Information Specialist (FaMI) Library Traineeship IT Specialist for System Integration IT Specialist for Application Development Teaching Mission Statement for Teaching Course Design Qualification and Continuing Education Teaching Advice and Service Teaching Organization Lecture Recordings Course Reserves Digital teaching Transfer International Teaching Teaching Abroad Online Exchange Initiative Funds and Awards Tag der Lehre Teaching Awards Lehre@ENGAGE.EU Fund “Innovative Digital Teaching” Fund Teaching Projects Hochschulweiterbildung@BW Sustainability Program for Visiting Scholars InnoMA PePP Data Literacy Information for Teachers The MaDaLi² Project E-learning course Mannheim Data Literacy (MaDaLi²) Service Learning Lehre @ ENGAGE.EU Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde der Universität Mannheim Other Foundations and Funding Honors Counseling and Services Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Intranet + Skip to main navigation Skip to page content Skip to footer Schools Department of Law Department of Economics Business School School of Social Sciences School of Humanities School of Business Informatics and Mathematics Search Barrierefreiheit EN DE EN Menu Credit: Staatliche Schlösser und Gärten Baden-Württemberg University About Working at the University Job Vacancies Data Protection in Job Applications Data Protection in Job Applications Information according to article 13 of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR): 1. Contact details of the controller The controller according to article 13 subsection 1(a) of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is the University of Mannheim L1, 1 68131 Mannheim Phone: 0621-181-1001 E-mail: rektor @ uni-mannheim.de 2. Contact details of the Data Protection Officer You can contact our Data Protection Officer at datenschutzbeauftragter @ uni-mannheim.de 3. Purpose and legal basis of data processing We process your application data in order to assess whether you have the required qualifications and aptitude and fulfill the professional requirements for the position you are applying for. The legal provisions for the selection process of the University of Mannheim in particular result from section 33 subsection 2 of the German Basic Law (GG), the General Act on Equal Treatment (AGG), and, if applicable, the act on the higher education institutions in the Land of Baden-Württemberg (LHG) and budgetary law. The legal basis for data processing in the selection process for the justification of a civil servant/ employment/internship is section 15 of the data protection act of the Land of Baden-Württemberg (LDSG) in conjunction with sections 83 to 85 of the civil service act of the Land of Baden-Württemberg (LGB). 4. Recipients of personal data The recipients of the personal data contained in the application documents are the responsible human resources managers as well as the staff representatives. In case of applications for professorships the group of recipients of personal data includes the responsible human resources managers, the members of the appointments committee and, where necessary, further persons such as evaluators or the representative for employees with a disability. Parts of the personal data may also be transferred to the university bodies involved in the appointment. 5. Storage period Your personal data/ application documents will be destroyed within three months after receipt of a rejection, unless longer storage is necessary in order to defend legal claims. In case the application process results in an employment contract of any kind for you, your data will be stored for the time being and transferred to the personnel file. 6. Rights of the data subject You have the right of access (article 15 of the General Data Protection Act (GDPR)) and the right to rectification (article 16 GDPR) or erasure (article 17 GDPR) as well as the right to restriction of processing (article 18 GDPR), the right to object (article 21 GDPR), and the right to data portability (article 20 GDPR). Furthermore, you have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority (article 77 GDPR). The responsible supervisory authority in Baden-Württemberg is the commissioner for data protection and freedom of information of Baden-Württemberg (Landesbeauftragter für den Datenschutz und die Informationsfreiheit Baden-Württemberg, LfDI). 7. Obligation to provide personal data In order for the selection process to be carried out as required by law, applicants are required to provide the relevant personal data. Applicants who fail to provide the relevant personal data might not be considered for the post/ position in question. The legal provisions for the selection process of the University of Mannheim in particular result from section 33 subsection 2 of the German Basic Law (GG), the General Act on Equal Treatment (AGG), and, if applicable, the act on the higher education institutions in the Land of Baden-Württemberg (LHG) and budgetary law. Accordingly, candidates must be selected based on their qualifications, aptitude, and professional requirements. Download: Data Protection in Job Applications ( PDF , 355 KB ) Seal of the University of Mannheim: In omnibus veritas + Application Programs Online Application Choosing a Program Financing + Campus Visit Map and Directions 3D Campus Tour Eating on Campus Events + Media Relations Media Contact Finding an Expert Recording Permissions Press Releases Newsletter + Go directly to ... Portal² Mannheim University Library University IT Employment Opportunities FORUM The University of Mannheim's magazine + Getting Involved University of Mannheim Foundation Freunde Universität Mannheim Absolventum Mannheim Scholarships Contact About This Site Data Protection Declaration Barrierefreiheit Sitemap House Rules Safety and Emergencies Instagram Page of the University of Mannheim Facebook Page of the University of Mannheim LinkedIn Page of the University of Mannheim Tiktok Page of the University of Mannheim YouTube Page of the University of Mannheim Mastodon Page of the University of Mannheim In order to improve performance and enhance the user experience for the visitors to our website, we use cookies and store anonymous usage data. For more information please read our privacy policy . Allow Reject Tracking cookies are currently allowed. Do not allow tracking cookies Tracking cookies are currently not allowed. Allow tracking cookies × How would you like to open the file? Remember for next time View PDF document Download PDF document"
    },
